## ⚠️ Limitations and Responsible Use

A credibility score is an estimate, not proof that a claim is true or false. Results depend on source quality, evidence availability, and model accuracy. Image manipulation screening may produce false positives or miss sophisticated edits.

The system should show citations where available, communicate uncertainty, and avoid presenting unverified conclusions as facts. Human review is recommended for high-impact decisions.

